<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Orléans</h1><p class="st-meta">511 CE – 524 CE · capital Orléans</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived Merovingian kingdom of Clovis' son Chlodomer, which vanished when he fell in battle in 524.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the division of 511 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a>' second son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer</a> received lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> as his capital, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bourges">Bourges</a> and part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer</a> ruled for only thirteen years. Little is known of his government beyond his wars against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-burgundians">Kingdom of the Burgundians</a>, during which he had the captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-of-burgundy">King Sigismund</a> and his family killed in 524.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer</a> was killed later in 524 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vezeronce">Battle of Vézeronce</a>. His uncles <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> murdered two of his young sons and divided his kingdom. The third son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clodoald">Clodoald</a>, escaped and became a monk; the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-cloud">Saint-Cloud</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> is named after him.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 511 CE – 524 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:69.87%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>511 CE – 524 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Orléans</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Chlodomer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Frankish, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=518&amp;focus=kingdom-of-orleans" aria-label="Kingdom of Orléans on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4724 500 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Orléans lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5044 756L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5044 756h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5044 756h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Orléans. <a href="/atlas?year=518&amp;focus=kingdom-of-orleans">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
